    {
      "id": "be-s12m-perfect-competition-c1",
      "heading": "The environment and its implications",
      "explanation_md": "**Perfect competition** has:\n\n- **Many buyers and sellers**\n- A **homogeneous (identical) product**\n- **Perfect information** on both sides\n- **No transaction costs**\n- **Free entry and exit**\n\n**Implications:** firms are **price takers (P = MR)**; in the **short run** they may earn **profits or losses**; **entry and exit force long-run profits to zero**.\n\n**Why learn it?** Many small businesses are price takers; it is a **useful benchmark**; it explains **why governments oppose monopolies**; and it shows the **danger** of competitive environments and the importance of **product differentiation** and **sustainable advantage**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Many firms, identical product, perfect information, no transaction costs, free entry: price takers with zero long-run profit.",
      "clarification": null,
