    {
      "id": "be-s12m-perfect-competition-c2",
      "heading": "Setting price and output",
      "explanation_md": "The **market** sets the price Pe where supply meets demand. The **firm** faces a **horizontal demand curve Df at Pe**: it can sell any amount at that price.\n\nProfit is maximized where **MR = MC**. Since **MR = P**, the rule becomes **P = MC**.\n\n**Profit = (Pe - ATC) x Qf***",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Price taker: set P = MC. Profit = (Pe - ATC) x Qf*.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
        {
          "id": "be-s12m-perfect-competition-q-25e3df07",
          "type": "mcq",
          "stem": "A perfectly competitive firm maximizes profit by producing where:",
          "options": [
